1
00:00:00,065 --> 00:00:05,584
Meet Aya (fictional): a beginner English learner with an old shared phone and no mobile data.

2
00:00:05,584 --> 00:00:11,391
Before: her teacher's lesson lives online. With no connection, she can't study at home at all.

3
00:00:11,391 --> 00:00:17,767
LessonPack: the teacher pastes a short lesson in plain text: words, a dialogue, questions.

4
00:00:17,767 --> 00:00:22,858
Simple format: 'word = meaning', 'Speaker: line = translation', '+' marks the right answer.

5
00:00:22,858 --> 00:00:29,099
One click (or Enter) makes ONE self-contained HTML file. No account, no server, no upload.

6
00:00:29,099 --> 00:00:34,594
24 KB. Send it by Bluetooth, USB cable, SD card or a chat app. It never needs the internet again.

7
00:00:34,594 --> 00:00:39,600
After: Aya opens the file with Wi-Fi and data off. Everything works.

8
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:46,113
Display options: larger text, high contrast, and easy-read spacing for dyslexic readers.

9
00:00:46,113 --> 00:00:51,262
Every word and line has a Listen button. It uses the phone's own offline voice, at normal or slow speed.

10
00:00:51,262 --> 00:00:56,344
If the phone has no speech engine, the buttons are hidden and a note says so. The text is always there.

11
00:00:56,344 --> 00:01:01,520
Translations can be hidden for self-testing. The page is all real headings, labels and buttons for screen readers.

12
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:06,376
Self-check quiz with immediate feedback, fully keyboard-operable.

13
00:01:06,376 --> 00:01:11,088
Wrong first? 'Not yet, try again' — after two tries it shows a hint from the dialogue.

14
00:01:11,088 --> 00:01:16,501
Typed answers are forgiving about capitals and punctuation.

15
00:01:16,501 --> 00:01:22,438
Progress is saved on the phone itself. Close the file, reopen it tomorrow: it is still there.

16
00:01:22,438 --> 00:01:27,983
Tested: axe-core 0 violations, keyboard-only walkthrough, 320px screens, JavaScript-off and no-speech fallbacks.

17
00:01:27,983 --> 00:01:33,014
LessonPack: one barrier removed. No data, no problem. Open source, MIT. class-now.github.io/lessonpack
